{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgVPt4fTJtU1dPoipFz4K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lqq6dTvYpoKyzmeJNHTz2M","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/enramosjr/Projects/agentic-assurance-7/docs/assurance/operator-2-mechanical-native-v5/git-metadata/okf-scratch/eval-attempt-mrg36_n0/repo/knowledge/history/named-greeting-plan.md","old_string":"# Named greeting plan\n\nImplementation plan for the named-greeting delta\n","new_string":"# Implementation Plan: Named greeting\n\n## Objective\n\nApply the approved named-greeting delta: `greet(name)` returns `'Hello, '` plus the supplied name.\n\n## Success criteria\n\n- GREET-R1: `greet` output starts with `Hello`; `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` passes.\n- GREET-R2: output includes the name after a comma and space; `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` passes.\n\n## Current state\n\n`util.py` defines `greet(name)` returning the constant `'hello'`. `test_greeting.py` already asserts `greet('Ada') == 'Hello, Ada'` and `greet('Bo') == 'Hello, Bo'`, so it fails now and is preserved unchanged.\n\n## Proposed approach\n\nChange the return expression in `util.py` to `'Hello, ' + name`. No contract beyond the delta, no dependencies.\n\n## Boundaries and invariants\n\nOnly `util.py` changes among application files. `test_greeting.py` is not edited.\n\n## Implementation steps\n\n### Step 1: Confirm red\n\nFiles: `test_greeting.py`. Run `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` and see it fail. Verification: nonzero exit (GREET-R1, GREET-R2).\n\n### Step 2: Make greet return the named greeting\n\nFiles: `util.py`, symbol `greet`. Return `'Hello, ' + name`. Verification: `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` passes (GREET-R1, GREET-R2).\n\n### Step 3: Fold the delta into the capability\n\nRun `lifecycle.py merge` on the spec, then sync OKF and log. Verification: `okf.py records` exits 0.\n\n## Testing strategy\n\nThe existing `test_greeting.py` covers both requirements with two names; no new tests.\n\n## Validation commands\n\n- Focused and slice E2E: `python3 -m unittest test_greeting`\n- Gate: `python3 .ai/scripts/okf.py records`\n\n## OKF impact\n\n`knowledge/capabilities/greeting.md` via delta merge; the spec status; `knowledge/log.md`.\n\n## Risks and mitigations\n\nNone material.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nOther utilities.\n\n## Open decisions\n\nNone. The plan is ready for implementation.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":350,"cache_read_input_tokens":47800,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":350},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb17d956-bfb8-4eec-b0d8-b8f57d1a5c97","uuid":"27bcef95-e2b9-4025-ad6d-b80df0871510","timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:06:39.569Z","request_id":"req_011CgVPt4V35FLBpDahWWNWN","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Lqq6dTvYpoKyzmeJNHTz2M":{"file_path":"/home/enramosjr/Projects/agentic-assurance-7/docs/assurance/operator-2-mechanical-native-v5/git-metadata/okf-scratch/eval-attempt-mrg36_n0/repo/knowledge/history/named-greeting-plan.md","old_string":"# Named greeting plan\n\nImplementation plan for the named-greeting delta\n","new_string":"# Implementation Plan: Named greeting\n\n## Objective\n\nApply the approved named-greeting delta: `greet(name)` returns `'Hello, '` plus the supplied name.\n\n## Success criteria\n\n- GREET-R1: `greet` output starts with `Hello`; `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` passes.\n- GREET-R2: output includes the name after a comma and space; `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` passes.\n\n## Current state\n\n`util.py` defines `greet(name)` returning the constant `'hello'`. `test_greeting.py` already asserts `greet('Ada') == 'Hello, Ada'` and `greet('Bo') == 'Hello, Bo'`, so it fails now and is preserved unchanged.\n\n## Proposed approach\n\nChange the return expression in `util.py` to `'Hello, ' + name`. No contract beyond the delta, no dependencies.\n\n## Boundaries and invariants\n\nOnly `util.py` changes among application files. `test_greeting.py` is not edited.\n\n## Implementation steps\n\n### Step 1: Confirm red\n\nFiles: `test_greeting.py`. Run `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` and see it fail. Verification: nonzero exit (GREET-R1, GREET-R2).\n\n### Step 2: Make greet return the named greeting\n\nFiles: `util.py`, symbol `greet`. Return `'Hello, ' + name`. Verification: `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` passes (GREET-R1, GREET-R2).\n\n### Step 3: Fold the delta into the capability\n\nRun `lifecycle.py merge` on the spec, then sync OKF and log. Verification: `okf.py records` exits 0.\n\n## Testing strategy\n\nThe existing `test_greeting.py` covers both requirements with two names; no new tests.\n\n## Validation commands\n\n- Focused and slice E2E: `python3 -m unittest test_greeting`\n- Gate: `python3 .ai/scripts/okf.py records`\n\n## OKF impact\n\n`knowledge/capabilities/greeting.md` via delta merge; the spec status; `knowledge/log.md`.\n\n## Risks and mitigations\n\nNone material.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nOther utilities.\n\n## Open decisions\n\nNone. The plan is ready for implementation.\n"}}}
