{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lqq6dTvYpoKyzmeJNHTz2M","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/enramosjr/Projects/agentic-assurance-7/docs/assurance/operator-2-mechanical-native-v5/git-metadata/okf-scratch/eval-attempt-mrg36_n0/repo/knowledge/history/named-greeting-plan.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb17d956-bfb8-4eec-b0d8-b8f57d1a5c97","uuid":"36b965b3-2887-4131-b468-5b062d3465b8","timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:06:39.762Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/home/enramosjr/Projects/agentic-assurance-7/docs/assurance/operator-2-mechanical-native-v5/git-metadata/okf-scratch/eval-attempt-mrg36_n0/repo/knowledge/history/named-greeting-plan.md","oldString":"# Named greeting plan\n\nImplementation plan for the named-greeting delta\n","newString":"# Implementation Plan: Named greeting\n\n## Objective\n\nApply the approved named-greeting delta: `greet(name)` returns `'Hello, '` plus the supplied name.\n\n## Success criteria\n\n- GREET-R1: `greet` output starts with `Hello`; `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` passes.\n- GREET-R2: output includes the name after a comma and space; `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` passes.\n\n## Current state\n\n`util.py` defines `greet(name)` returning the constant `'hello'`. `test_greeting.py` already asserts `greet('Ada') == 'Hello, Ada'` and `greet('Bo') == 'Hello, Bo'`, so it fails now and is preserved unchanged.\n\n## Proposed approach\n\nChange the return expression in `util.py` to `'Hello, ' + name`. No contract beyond the delta, no dependencies.\n\n## Boundaries and invariants\n\nOnly `util.py` changes among application files. `test_greeting.py` is not edited.\n\n## Implementation steps\n\n### Step 1: Confirm red\n\nFiles: `test_greeting.py`. Run `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` and see it fail. Verification: nonzero exit (GREET-R1, GREET-R2).\n\n### Step 2: Make greet return the named greeting\n\nFiles: `util.py`, symbol `greet`. Return `'Hello, ' + name`. Verification: `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` passes (GREET-R1, GREET-R2).\n\n### Step 3: Fold the delta into the capability\n\nRun `lifecycle.py merge` on the spec, then sync OKF and log. Verification: `okf.py records` exits 0.\n\n## Testing strategy\n\nThe existing `test_greeting.py` covers both requirements with two names; no new tests.\n\n## Validation commands\n\n- Focused and slice E2E: `python3 -m unittest test_greeting`\n- Gate: `python3 .ai/scripts/okf.py records`\n\n## OKF impact\n\n`knowledge/capabilities/greeting.md` via delta merge; the spec status; `knowledge/log.md`.\n\n## Risks and mitigations\n\nNone material.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nOther utilities.\n\n## Open decisions\n\nNone. The plan is ready for implementation.\n","originalFile":"---\ntype: Plan\ntitle: Named greeting plan\ndescription: Implementation plan for the named-greeting delta\ntags: []\nstatus: draft\nevidence: project-documentation\ngenerated: { by: agent/unknown, at: 2026-10-28T22:06:32Z }\nsources:\n  - id: util-py\n    resource: ../../util.py\n  - id: test-greeting-py\n    resource: ../../test_greeting.py\n---\n\n# Named greeting plan\n\nImplementation plan for the named-greeting delta\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":13,"oldLines":6,"newStart":13,"newLines":64,"lines":["     resource: ../../test_greeting.py"," ---"," ","-# Named greeting plan","+# Implementation Plan: Named greeting"," ","-Implementation plan for the named-greeting delta","+## Objective","+","+Apply the approved named-greeting delta: `greet(name)` returns `'Hello, '` plus the supplied name.","+","+## Success criteria","+","+- GREET-R1: `greet` output starts with `Hello`; `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` passes.","+- GREET-R2: output includes the name after a comma and space; `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` passes.","+","+## Current state","+","+`util.py` defines `greet(name)` returning the constant `'hello'`. `test_greeting.py` already asserts `greet('Ada') == 'Hello, Ada'` and `greet('Bo') == 'Hello, Bo'`, so it fails now and is preserved unchanged.","+","+## Proposed approach","+","+Change the return expression in `util.py` to `'Hello, ' + name`. No contract beyond the delta, no dependencies.","+","+## Boundaries and invariants","+","+Only `util.py` changes among application files. `test_greeting.py` is not edited.","+","+## Implementation steps","+","+### Step 1: Confirm red","+","+Files: `test_greeting.py`. Run `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` and see it fail. Verification: nonzero exit (GREET-R1, GREET-R2).","+","+### Step 2: Make greet return the named greeting","+","+Files: `util.py`, symbol `greet`. Return `'Hello, ' + name`. Verification: `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` passes (GREET-R1, GREET-R2).","+","+### Step 3: Fold the delta into the capability","+","+Run `lifecycle.py merge` on the spec, then sync OKF and log. Verification: `okf.py records` exits 0.","+","+## Testing strategy","+","+The existing `test_greeting.py` covers both requirements with two names; no new tests.","+","+## Validation commands","+","+- Focused and slice E2E: `python3 -m unittest test_greeting`","+- Gate: `python3 .ai/scripts/okf.py records`","+","+## OKF impact","+","+`knowledge/capabilities/greeting.md` via delta merge; the spec status; `knowledge/log.md`.","+","+## Risks and mitigations","+","+None material.","+","+## Out of scope","+","+Other utilities.","+","+## Open decisions","+","+None. The plan is ready for implementation."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Lqq6dTvYpoKyzmeJNHTz2M","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
