{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EqSEZcdeWQU59Lqkgs6Fbx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\ttype: Plan\n3\ttitle: Named greeting plan\n4\tdescription: Implementation plan for the named-greeting delta\n5\ttags: []\n6\tstatus: draft\n7\tevidence: project-documentation\n8\tgenerated: { by: agent/unknown, at: 2026-10-28T22:06:32Z }\n9\tsources:\n10\t  - id: util-py\n11\t    resource: ../../util.py\n12\t  - id: test-greeting-py\n13\t    resource: ../../test_greeting.py\n14\tverified: { by: \"process:python3 -m unittest test_greeting\", at: 2026-10-28T22:06:59Z }\n15\t---\n16\t\n17\t# Implementation Plan: Named greeting\n18\t\n19\t## Objective\n20\t\n21\tApply the approved named-greeting delta: `greet(name)` returns `'Hello, '` plus the supplied name.\n22\t\n23\t## Success criteria\n24\t\n25\t- GREET-R1: `greet` output starts with `Hello`; `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` passes.\n26\t- GREET-R2: output includes the name after a comma and space; `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` passes.\n27\t\n28\t## Current state\n29\t\n30\t`util.py` defines `greet(name)` returning the constant `'hello'`. `test_greeting.py` already asserts `greet('Ada') == 'Hello, Ada'` and `greet('Bo') == 'Hello, Bo'`, so it fails now and is preserved unchanged.\n31\t\n32\t## Proposed approach\n33\t\n34\tChange the return expression in `util.py` to `'Hello, ' + name`. No contract beyond the delta, no dependencies.\n35\t\n36\t## Boundaries and invariants\n37\t\n38\tOnly `util.py` changes among application files. `test_greeting.py` is not edited.\n39\t\n40\t## Implementation steps\n41\t\n42\t### Step 1: Confirm red\n43\t\n44\tFiles: `test_greeting.py`. Run `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` and see it fail. Verification: nonzero exit (GREET-R1, GREET-R2).\n45\t\n46\t### Step 2: Make greet return the named greeting\n47\t\n48\tFiles: `util.py`, symbol `greet`. Return `'Hello, ' + name`. Verification: `python3 -m unittest test_greeting` passes (GREET-R1, GREET-R2).\n49\t\n50\t### Step 3: Fold the delta into the capability\n51\t\n52\tRun `lifecycle.py merge` on the spec, then sync OKF and log. Verification: `okf.py records` exits 0.\n53\t\n54\t## Testing strategy\n55\t\n56\tThe existing `test_greeting.py` covers both requirements with two names; no new tests.\n57\t\n58\t## Validation commands\n59\t\n60\t- Focused and slice E2E: `python3 -m unittest test_greeting`\n61\t- Gate: `python3 .ai/scripts/okf.py records`\n62\t\n63\t## OKF impact\n64\t\n65\t`knowledge/capabilities/greeting.md` via delta merge; the spec status; `knowledge/log.md`.\n66\t\n67\t## Risks and mitigations\n68\t\n69\tNone material.\n70\t\n71\t## Out of scope\n72\t\n73\tOther utilities.\n74\t\n75\t## Open decisions\n76\t\n77\tNone. The plan is ready for implementation.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01S6HuJy8syzJA6uYHPqRdfc","agent_id":"a9593c0b452281b45","session_id":"bb17d956-bfb8-4eec-b0d8-b8f57d1a5c97","uuid":"3aa1bc7e-9748-4e1e-9717-38716e207598","timestamp":"2026-10-28T22:07:15.591Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EqSEZcdeWQU59Lqkgs6Fbx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"reviewer","task_description":"Independent native review"}
